      "avg_processing_time": 12.57631862640381
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0015",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0015.flac",
      "reference": "IT WAS PRODUCED ON ONE HAND BY THE NATURAL GROWTH OF POPULATION AND ON THE OTHER BY STRUGGLE AND CONQUEST",
      "hypothesis": "It was produced on one hand by the natural growth of population and on the other by struggle and conquest.",
      "duration": 6.44,
      "total_time": 20.520663261413574,
      "first_token_latency": 0.927403450012207,
      "avg_processing_time": 14.080663261413573
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0016",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0016.flac",
      "reference": "AFTER CONQUEST THE POWER OF THE EMPEROR PUTS AN END TO INTERNAL DISSENSIONS AND SO THE STATE CONCEPTION OF LIFE JUSTIFIES ITSELF",
      "hypothesis": "After conquest,, the power of the emperor puts an end to internal dissensions, and so the state conception of life justifies itself.",
      "duration": 7.47,
      "total_time": 21.123375415802002,
      "first_token_latency": 1.2145910263061523,
      "avg_processing_time": 13.653375415802003
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0018",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0018.flac",
      "reference": "INTERNAL DISSENSIONS DISAPPEAR ONLY IN PROPORTION TO THE DEGREE OF OPPRESSION EXERTED BY THE AUTHORITY OVER THE DISSENTIENT INDIVIDUALS",
      "hypothesis": "Internal dissensions disappear only in proportion to the degree of oppression exerted by the authority over the dissentient individuals.",
      "duration": 7.095,
      "total_time": 20.97338581085205,
      "first_token_latency": 1.0423669815063477,
      "avg_processing_time": 13.878385810852052
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0019",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0019.flac",
      "reference": "GOVERNMENT AUTHORITY EVEN IF IT DOES SUPPRESS PRIVATE VIOLENCE ALWAYS INTRODUCES INTO THE LIFE OF MEN FRESH FORMS OF VIOLENCE WHICH TEND TO BECOME GREATER AND GREATER IN PROPORTION TO THE DURATION AND STRENGTH OF THE GOVERNMENT",
      "hypothesis": "government authority, even if it does suppress private violence, always introduces into the life of men fresh forms of violence, which tend to become greater and greater in proportion to the duration and strength of the government.",
      "duration": 11.72,
      "total_time": 21.522608041763306,
      "first_token_latency": 1.8833448886871338,
      "avg_processing_time": 9.802608041763305
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0021",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0021.flac",
      "reference": "THE MOST CONVINCING EXAMPLE OF THIS IS TO BE FOUND IN THE CONDITION OF THE WORKING CLASSES OF OUR EPOCH WHO ARE IN REALITY NO BETTER THAN THE SLAVES OF ANCIENT TIMES SUBDUED BY CONQUEST",
      "hypothesis": "The most convincing example of this is to be found in the condition of the working classes of our epoch, who are in reality no better than the slaves of ancient times subdued by conquest.",
      "duration": 9.565,
      "total_time": 21.426172256469727,
      "first_token_latency": 1.400820255279541,
      "avg_processing_time": 11.861172256469727
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0023",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0023.flac",
      "reference": "FOOTNOTE THE FACT THAT IN AMERICA THE ABUSES OF AUTHORITY EXIST IN SPITE OF THE SMALL NUMBER OF THEIR TROOPS NOT ONLY FAILS TO DISPROVE THIS POSITION BUT POSITIVELY CONFIRMS IT",
      "hypothesis": "footnotes. The fact that in America the abuses of authority exist in spite of the small number of their troops not only fails to disprove this position but positively confirms it.",
      "duration": 9.5,
      "total_time": 21.315218210220337,
      "first_token_latency": 1.6913604736328125,
      "avg_processing_time": 11.815218210220337
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0024",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0024.flac",
      "reference": "THE UPPER CLASSES KNOW THAT AN ARMY OF FIFTY THOUSAND WILL SOON BE INSUFFICIENT AND NO LONGER RELYING ON PINKERTON'S MEN THEY FEEL THAT THE SECURITY OF THEIR POSITION DEPENDS ON THE INCREASED STRENGTH OF THE ARMY",
      "hypothesis": "The upper classes know that an army of 50,000 will soon be insufficient and, no longer relying on Pinkertons men, they feel that the security of their position depends on the increased strength of the army.",
      "duration": 9.89,
      "total_time": 21.1144700050354,
      "first_token_latency": 1.1872870922088623,
      "avg_processing_time": 11.2244700050354
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0033",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0033.flac",
      "reference": "THE RIVALRY OF THE EUROPEAN STATES IN CONSTANTLY INCREASING THEIR FORCES HAS REDUCED THEM TO THE NECESSITY OF HAVING RECOURSE TO UNIVERSAL MILITARY SERVICE SINCE BY THAT MEANS THE GREATEST POSSIBLE NUMBER OF SOLDIERS IS OBTAINED AT THE LEAST POSSIBLE EXPENSE",
      "hypothesis": "The rivalry of the European states in constantly increasing their forces has reduced them to the necessity of having recourse to universal military service, since by that means the greatest possible number of soldiers is obtained at the least possible expense.",
      "duration": 13.17,
      "total_time": 21.23317050933838,
      "first_token_latency": 1.3110673427581787,
      "avg_processing_time": 8.063170509338379
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0034",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0034.flac",
      "reference": "AND BY THIS MEANS ALL CITIZENS ARE UNDER ARMS TO SUPPORT THE INIQUITIES PRACTICED UPON THEM ALL CITIZENS HAVE BECOME THEIR OWN OPPRESSORS",
      "hypothesis": "And by this means all citizens are under arms to support the iniquities practiced upon them. All citizens have become their own oppressors.",
      "duration": 7.185,
      "total_time": 21.079177379608154,
      "first_token_latency": 1.156869888305664,
      "avg_processing_time": 13.894177379608156
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0036",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0036.flac",
      "reference": "IN FACT THE WHOLE SIGNIFICANCE OF THE SOCIAL CONCEPTION OF LIFE CONSISTS IN MAN'S RECOGNITION OF THE BARBARITY OF STRIFE BETWEEN INDIVIDUALS AND THE TRANSITORINESS OF PERSONAL LIFE ITSELF AND THE TRANSFERENCE OF THE AIM OF LIFE TO GROUPS OF PERSONS",
      "hypothesis": "In fact, the whole significance of the social conception of life consists in man's recognition of the barbarity of strife between individuals, and the transitoriness of personal life itself, and the transference of the aim of life to groups of persons.",
      "duration": 13.525,
      "total_time": 21.287031650543213,
      "first_token_latency": 1.6612474918365479,
      "avg_processing_time": 7.7620316505432125
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0039",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0039.flac",
      "reference": "THE TAXES RAISED FROM THE PEOPLE FOR WAR PREPARATIONS ABSORB THE GREATER PART OF THE PRODUCE OF LABOR WHICH THE ARMY OUGHT TO DEFEND",
      "hypothesis": "The taxes raised from the people for war preparations absorb the greater part of the produce of labor which the army ought to defend.",
      "duration": 6.875,
      "total_time": 21.278820037841797,
      "first_token_latency": 1.2521092891693115,
      "avg_processing_time": 14.403820037841797
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0040",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0040.flac",
      "reference": "THE DANGER OF WAR EVER READY TO BREAK OUT RENDERS ALL REFORMS OF LIFE SOCIAL LIFE VAIN AND FRUITLESS",
      "hypothesis": "The danger of war, ever ready to break out, renders all reforms of life's social life vain and fruitless.",
      "duration": 6.28,
      "total_time": 20.560433864593506,
      "first_token_latency": 0.9489343166351318,
      "avg_processing_time": 14.280433864593505
    },
    {
      "file_id": "4350-9170-0042",
      "speaker_id": "4350",
      "audio_path": "c:\\Users\\VRSTUDIO3\\Desktop\\STiTy-main1\\LibriSpeech\\test-other\\4350\\9170\\4350-9170-0042.flac",
      "reference": "GOVERNMENTS ASSERT THAT ARMIES ARE NEEDED ABOVE ALL FOR EXTERNAL DEFENSE BUT THAT IS NOT TRUE",
      "hypothesis": "Governments assert that armies are needed above all for external defense, but that is not true.",
